      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2017, the FCC concluded that three of its ownership rules were no longer necessary to promote competition, localism, or viewpoint diversity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Third Circuit",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Third Circuit vacated the FCC's reconsideration order, holding that the record did not support the agency's conclusion that the rule changes would have minimal effect on minority and female ownership."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Prometheus Radio Project",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In challenging the FCC's order, Prometheus argues that the Commission's assessment of the likely impact of the rule changes on minority and female ownership rested on fawed data."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Prometheus Radio Project",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Prometheus also asserts that the FCC ignored two studies submitted by a commenter that purported to show that past relaxations of the ownership rules had led to decreases in minority and female ownership levels."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Prometheus",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Prometheus asserts that the FCC relied on fawed data in assessing the likely impact of changing the rules on minority and female ownership. Prometheus further argues that the FCC ignored superior data available in the record."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Based on the record, the Commission concluded that repealing or modifying the three rules was not likely to harm minority and female ownership. See id., at 9822, 9830, 9839."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Prometheus",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Prometheus also asserts that countervailing\u2014and superior\u2014evidence was in fact in the record, and that the FCC ignored that evidence. Prometheus identifes two studies submitted to the FCC by Free Press, a media reform group."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f55df67f10c6598b64add503dbb460b472e5c90cdf2df518e7d98a5eefbf055d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f55df67f10c6-0001-0003",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "agency's decision to repeal or modify the ownership rules fell outside the zone of reasonableness for purposes of the APA."
    }
  ],
